  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Cambio Clim&#xe1;tico - Paisajes Sostenibles</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kalan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Mexico):  With FY 2024 funds, USAID&apos;s Kalan activity will build the capacity of the GOM and local communities in biodiversity conservation, forest management, and governance to expand and conserve critical biodiversity habitat in the Selva Maya of southern Mexico, as well as reduce deforestation via sustainable natural resource management. The activity will also help conserve natural areas that are important to species that migrate between the United States and Mexico. The expected main GOM counterparts are Mexico&apos;s Natural Protected Areas Commission (CONANP) and its Forestry Commission (CONAFOR). The funds will support GOM efforts to sustainably manage their federal and state protected areas while also working with local communities, many of them indigenous, on conservation priorities. Over the life of the activity, Kalan will directly catalyze up to $180 million in additional resources to support Mexico&apos;s 30 x 30 goal. This activity aligns with ICS Mission Objective 3.1 and contributes to the following key issues: Biodiversity, Sustainable Landscapes Direct and Indirect, Combating Wildlife Trafficking, and Partnership for Global Infrastructure Indirect - Climate.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Garantizar que el medio ambiente y los recursos naturales de los que dependen las vidas y los medios de subsistencia humanos se gestionen de manera que sostengan la productividad y el crecimiento, as&#xed; como una poblaci&#xf3;n sana.</narrative>
  </description>
